Makefile.libretro forwards OVERRIDE_CC/OVERRIDE_CXX to MAME's genie build only
on the Windows, Apple and webOS branches.  On Linux nothing is forwarded, so
genie falls back to plain `gcc`/`g++` and the whole core is built with the BUILD
HOST's compiler -- the cross toolchain in CC/CXX is silently ignored.  On an
x86_64 host that yields an x86 core; on an aarch64 host (Apple Silicon/OrbStack)
it compiles, but against the host glibc and without the profile's wrapper flags,
and the final link of the full 43k-driver core then overflows R_AARCH64_CALL26.

Same opt-in as patches/_common/same_cdi/0001 (a MAME fork with the same
Makefile.libretro lineage): when CROSS_BUILD is set, pass the compilers through,
plus the two values genie otherwise derives from the build host -- PLATFORM
(from `uname -m`) and ARCHITECTURE (_x64 -> -m64, which aarch64 gcc rejects).
Guarded by ifneq, so a native build is unaffected.

diff --git a/Makefile.libretro b/Makefile.libretro
index 3799635e..75772efb 100644
--- a/Makefile.libretro
+++ b/Makefile.libretro
@@ -306,6 +306,11 @@ endif
 ifneq ($(LIBRETRO_CPU),)
 	PLATFLAGS += LIBRETRO_CPU=$(LIBRETRO_CPU)
 endif
+ifneq ($(CROSS_BUILD),)
+	PLATFLAGS += OVERRIDE_CC="$(CC)" OVERRIDE_CXX="$(CXX)"
+	PLATFLAGS += CROSS_BUILD="$(CROSS_BUILD)"
+	PLATFLAGS += PLATFORM="$(LIBRETRO_CPU)" ARCHITECTURE=""
+endif
 ifneq ($(FORCE_DRC_C_BACKEND),)
 	PLATFLAGS += FORCE_DRC_C_BACKEND=$(FORCE_DRC_C_BACKEND)
 endif
